  data: {
    LLM: "Starting hand selection is critical. A pair, a 4-flush draw, or 4-straight draw are playable. High cards are valuable. With the extra rankings, draws are more powerful than in regular Stud.\n\nRecognize that a 4-flush or 4-straight is often a winning hand against a single pair. However, Two Pair is still a very strong hand. Bluffing opportunities increase because a board showing 3 flush cards represents a likely 4-flush (a made hand).\n\nPot odds calculation must include the 4-card outs. Semi-bluffing with 3-card flush/straight draws on 3rd street is viable. Read the opponent's board: if they can't have a 4-card hand or pair, aggressive betting is key.",
    Player: "Starting hand selection is critical. A pair, a 4-flush draw, or 4-straight draw are playable. High cards are valuable. With the extra rankings, draws are more powerful than in regular Stud.\n\nRecognize that a 4-flush or 4-straight is often a winning hand against a single pair. However, Two Pair is still a very strong hand. Bluffing opportunities increase because a board showing 3 flush cards represents a likely 4-flush (a made hand).\n\nPot odds calculation must include the 4-card outs. Semi-bluffing with 3-card flush/straight draws on 3rd street is viable. Read the opponent's board: if they can't have a 4-card hand or pair, aggressive betting is key.",
